WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.140
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:14.540
The reading from the Sinaxadion for September 11 on which we commemorate our Holy Father

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.760
Ephrosinos, the cook.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.280
Saint Ephrosinos was a simple, minded peasant who took refuge in a monastery where he

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:31.360
was put to work in the kitchen as a schoolyon, doing the most thankless tasks.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:40.040
He became the laughingstock of everyone, but bore it all with unshakable generosity of spirit.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.000
There was a godly priest in the monastery who fervently desired that the Savior revealed

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.840
to him the good things he has in store for those who love him.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:58.720
One night, as he slept, he had the sense of being carried to paradise into a garden full

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.680
of unutterable delights.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:08.920
Ephrosinos was in the middle of the garden, tasting of the good things there and rejoicing

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.880
with the angels.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.120
The priest went up to him and asked where they were.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.600
Ephrosinos answered,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:26.360
This is the dwelling place of God's elect that you have long to see for so many years.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:33.320
And I am here because in his good pleasure God has forgiven my sins.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:39.360
Gazing upon those unutterable good things that I has not seen nor ear heard neither have

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:46.000
entered into the heart of man, the priest observed that they were to some extent perceptible to

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.000
those who dwelt there.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
So he asked Ephrosinos if he might take some of the fruit of the garden away with him,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.240
whereupon Ephrosinos took three apples and put them in the priest's cloak.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.720
Just then he was woken up by the sound of the call to matins.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.720
As he came to himself from what he thought was a dream, he was amazed to find three apples

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.120
in his cloak, giving off a scent of unearthly sweetness.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:24.320
He saw Ephrosinos in his usual place in the church and went up to him, begging him to

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.200
tell him where he had been during the night that it just passed.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:36.640
Forgive me, Father, he answered, but I have been here all the time.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.800
But as the devout priest pressed him earnestly not to conceal the blessings of God, the humble

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.840
Ephrosinos at last said,

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:52.320
It is true, Father, that I was in the garden where you saw the good things God has in store

00:02:52.320 --> 00:03:02.960
for his elect and that it was the Lord's wish to show you this mystery through my unworthiness.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:09.120
It was not long before the priest told everyone what he had witnessed and showed the apples

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.200
by way of proof.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.680
The monks were encouraged through this sign to follow all the more zealously the path

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:23.480
of virtue and those who tasted the apples were healed of all kinds of disease.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.960
As for the blessed Ephrosinos, he fled from the monastery.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:36.060
For there was nothing he feared more than the praise of men.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:42.380
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.380
and save us.
